event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission: greet, tested — summary\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` defines `greet(name)` returning `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` contains `TestGreet` with two cases:\\n   - `test_normal_name` — `greet(\\\"Alice\\\") == \\\"Hello, Alice!\\\"`\\n   - `test_empty_string` — `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (2 tests, OK).\\n\\n## How it was verified\\n\\nWork was dispatched to `dev` (d002). Dev implemented both files, committed to\\nits own branch (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit `44ed3b1`),\\nand reported the unittest command passing.\\n\\nRather than trusting the report, the orchestrator:\\n- Fetched dev's branch (`cs-campaign-member fetch dev subject`), confirming\\n  the tree differs from base with real changes.\\n- Inspected the diff directly (`git diff master refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`).\\n- Cloned the repo into an isolated temp directory, checked out commit\\n  `44ed3b1`, and independently ran `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`,\\n  observing exit code 0.\\n\\nDev's reply was accepted (`cs-campaign-member accept dev`) only after this\\nindependent verification succeeded.\\n\\n## Branch state\\n\\nThe orchestrator's own branch\\n(`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`) has no source changes —\\nby design, the orchestrator writes no code. All implementation work lives on\\ndev's branch, which is where the delivered `src/greet.py` and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` reside.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

event: content_block_stop
data: {"type":"content_block_stop","index":1      }

